  "body": "The maintainer reported this in chat on 2026-11-15, with a screenshot of the top of the main window.\n\nTwo defects, one fix:\n\n1. The mode tabs (MILLING, TURNING, MILL-TURNING, PLASMA CUTTING, WIRE EDM) moved above the ribbon. The tab row does not have sufficient height. The top of the tab text touches the window edge, and the underline of the active tab touches the ribbon.\n2. The ribbon icons (New, Model, Open, Save, Save As, Post, Setups, Stock, Origin, Tools) are blue on the gray bar. The contrast is too low to read them.\n\nThe maintainer's words: \"the tabs, milling, turning, millturning, etc etc.. moved above the ribbon, but doesnt have enough space.\" and \"turn the icons back to white.. Nobody can see blue on gray.\"\n\nExpected:\n\n- The tab row has its own height with space above and below the text, as the other tab bars of the application have.\n- The ribbon icons are white again, as before the change. The coloured operation icons (2D, 3D, Drill, Multi) keep their colours unless they changed in the same commit.\n\nFor the work:\n\n- Find the commit that moved the tabs and the commit that made the icons blue. Name them in the PR.\n- Obey `crates/ui/AGENTS.md`. Update the structural assertions, not the snapshot PNGs.\n- The PR body has a before and an after screenshot of the ribbon.\n\nDone means:\n\n- The tab text has clear space above and below at the default window size and at the smallest supported width.\n- The file and setup icons of the ribbon are white on the gray bar.\n- A structural test pins the height of the tab row or its position against the ribbon.\n",
